{title: Jesus Shall Reign}
{artist: Isaac Watts / John Hatton}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: jesus-shall-reign.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Jesus shall reign where'er the [G]sun
[D]Does its successive [A]journeys [D]run
His [D]kingdom spread from [G]shore to shore
[D]Till moons shall [A]wax and wane no [D]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]To Him shall endless [G]prayer be made
[D]And praises throng to [A]crown His [D]head
His [D]name like sweet per[G]fume shall rise
[D]With every [A]morning sacri[D]fice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]People and realms of [G]every tongue
[D]Dwell on His love with [A]sweetest [D]song
And [D]infant voices [G]shall proclaim
[D]Their early [A]blessings on His [D]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Blessings abound wher[G]ever He reigns
[D]The prisoner leaps to [A]lose his [D]chains
The [D]weary find e[G]ternal rest
And [D]all the sons of [A]want are [D]blessed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Let every creature [G]rise and bring
[D]Peculiar honors [A]to our [D]King
An[D]gels descend with [G]songs again
And [D]earth repeat the [A]loud A[D]men
{end_of_verse}
